WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.862
In Fractured Order, the Blue Scribe records the

00:00:02.862 --> 00:00:04.312
team's decision.

00:00:04.312 --> 00:00:07.062
The Facilitator submits it to White Cell.

00:00:07.062 --> 00:00:10.512
Your first task is to record Strategic Orientation and

00:00:10.512 --> 00:00:12.225
verify the handoff.

00:00:12.225 --> 00:00:15.113
Use a separate training Session with an assigned Blue

00:00:15.113 --> 00:00:18.150
Scribe seat and a receiving Facilitator.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:21.325
This guide uses AI-generated narration.

00:00:21.733 --> 00:00:24.721
On Join Session, enter the supplied Session Code

00:00:24.721 --> 00:00:26.733
and your agreed Display Name.

00:00:26.733 --> 00:00:29.783
Select Check session, choose Blue and Scribe,

00:00:29.783 --> 00:00:31.771
then select Join Session.

00:00:31.771 --> 00:00:33.958
Confirm your team and role.

00:00:33.958 --> 00:00:36.583
Start Here provides role-specific help.

00:00:36.583 --> 00:00:39.733
If the seat is occupied, contact the Operator

00:00:39.733 --> 00:00:39.871
.

00:00:39.871 --> 00:00:42.658
Do not take the Facilitator seat as a workaround

00:00:42.658 --> 00:00:42.833
.

00:00:43.233 --> 00:00:45.533
Open Strategic Orientation.

00:00:45.533 --> 00:00:48.783
First, choose the catalogue orientation Blue has agreed

00:00:48.783 --> 00:00:49.933
to pursue.

00:00:49.933 --> 00:00:52.858
Next, forecast Red's orientation.

00:00:52.858 --> 00:00:54.633
These are different judgments.

00:00:54.633 --> 00:00:57.283
Finally, describe what you expect Red to do

00:00:57.283 --> 00:00:58.883
under that forecast.

00:00:58.883 --> 00:01:02.358
Read the catalogue descriptions and use the team's brief

00:01:02.358 --> 00:01:02.495
.

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:05.020
Pause to check that the three entries express the

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:06.408
team's decision.

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:09.446
Select Record Strategic Orientation.

00:01:09.446 --> 00:01:12.820
Complete any missing field identified by the form.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:16.308
After saving, look for Strategic Orientation forwarded to

00:01:16.308 --> 00:01:19.133
Facilitator and the orientation card.

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:22.696
Check the saved choices and expected-action description.

00:01:22.696 --> 00:01:24.758
A toast alone is not enough.

00:01:24.758 --> 00:01:27.533
If an error appears, inspect the action list

00:01:27.533 --> 00:01:30.283
before resubmitting, then ask for help if the

00:01:30.283 --> 00:01:32.008
result is unclear.

00:01:32.433 --> 00:01:35.720
Ask the assigned Facilitator to confirm receipt in Team

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.095
Action Review.

00:01:37.095 --> 00:01:39.996
The Facilitator reviews and submits the record to White

00:01:39.996 --> 00:01:40.933
Cell.

00:01:40.933 --> 00:01:43.883
Forwarded to Facilitator does not mean White Cell has

00:01:43.883 --> 00:01:47.108
received, accepted, or completed it.

00:01:47.108 --> 00:01:49.733
It also does not authorize your team to advance

00:01:49.733 --> 00:01:50.920
to Move One.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:54.183
The handoff and the final review are separate stages

00:01:54.183 --> 00:01:54.333
.

00:01:54.742 --> 00:01:57.404
For an independent attempt, ask the Facilitator for

00:01:57.404 --> 00:01:59.967
a different training brief and a reset or separate

00:01:59.967 --> 00:02:00.979
Session.

00:02:00.979 --> 00:02:03.380
Record the new own choice, forecast, and

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:06.030
expected action without step prompts.

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:08.892
Show the saved inputs, verify the handoff,

00:02:08.892 --> 00:02:11.017
and explain who acts next.

00:02:11.017 --> 00:02:14.380
Success is a correctly recorded team decision reaching the

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:17.567
right person, not merely completing a form.
